      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "TLDR: to fix do these 2 steps.\n1. On the VRC_Scene Descriptor set the Reference Camera property to the Main Camera\n2. For the Main camera set the Near Clipping Plane distance to 0 (or something absurdly small)\n@{5f2cc4c9e078064277ef813a|full_name}, this can be set up in unity. Unfortunately it's quite easy to mess it up. And it's even more difficult figure out what's happening. I assume you dragged a camera onto the Reference Camera property of the VRC_Scene Descriptor. Highly likely it was the Main Camera that you assigned. If you did that then you'll have to select that camera and set the Near Clipping Plane distance to 0. Unity will replace it to something really small like 0.01.\nA bit of extra information about these worlds as there are 3 kinds of worlds: good, bad, and what I call neutral\n- good ones will set your eye camera clipping distance to 0\n- bad ones will set your eye camera quite a few centimiters away from your eyes\n- neutral worlds will remember the settings from the previous world you just came from\nThe good worlds will have the Reference camera set and have it's near clipping plane distance set to 0\nThe bad worlds will have the Reference camera set but the near clipping plane distance is left at the default value of 0.3 (IIRC)\nThe neutral worlds don't have the Reference camera set. This is how a new unity project starts by default",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-02-10T15:23:40.126Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Title: When creating a new SDK2 world (not sure with SDK3) player viewpoint is too far forward by a few cm.\nDescription:\nWhen creating a new SDK2 world (not sure with SDK3) player viewpoint is too far forward by a few cm.\nExpected: The viewpoint would be identical to older worlds (closer to the 'head')\nActual: The viewpoint is further ahead\nIssue was originally found in a world I was working on, tested on two different machines with entirely new projects consisting of just a plane and vrcworld prefab set at 0,0,0.",
